        {
          "path": "_m/w/w/7/r/four-gates-pagoda-wp/jinan-2009-1194.jpg",
          "filename": "Jinan 2009 1194.jpg",
          "caption": "Statue of Amitabha. Eastern Wei, 544 AD. Simen Ta, Jinan\nThe pagoda has a square central pillar, symbolizing the world-axis; around this, and facing outward through the doors to the four cardinal directions, are the directional buddhas: Amitabha (Amitayus, West), Amoghasiddhi (North), Akshobhya (East), and Ratnasambhava (South). Shown here is Amitabha, facing west.",
          "alt": "Statue of Amitabha. Eastern Wei, 544 AD. Simen Ta, Jinan\nThe pagoda has a square central pillar, symbolizing the world-axis; around this, and facing outward through the doors to the four cardinal directions, are the directional buddhas: Amitabha (Amitayus, West), Amoghasiddhi (North), Akshobhya (East), and Ratnasambhava (South). Shown here is Amitabha, facing west.",
